  triage:title "atm templates CLI command reads run on the writer-side control_path_pool" ;
  triage:description "fenix writer-pool audit V5: crates/atm/src/commands/templates.rs:36-64,89. A CLI list/show command reading the template catalog for display -- content-addressed by sha per 01M1T3THS8P4JDMGR3M6D2HSV2, so immutable and never RMW-eligible; it belongs on the read pool, tool-class capped (this is a diagnostics/inspection-style command, not agent send/read traffic). Severity important (fenix's proposal): a CLI-only, low-frequency path, correctness-neutral today, but it currently reads through the same writer-side pool AW-POOL-V9 removes." ;
